blic","site_admin":false},"body":"I've found that i need to do quite a lot of distance checking in projects and i got fed up with writing `node.global_position.distance_to(target.global_position)` every time i wanted to do this and there wasn't a method of doing it in GDScript that felt clean and compact enough. \r\n\r\ni looked around before going down this path and i couldn't find anything that really did this, wrapper functions and different formatting in GDScript made it slightly cleaner but i decided to go with putting these directly into the Node classes themselves to make it cleaner and more straight forward. they seem to work fine in my testing though I'm a little pessimistic on my implementation, i don't use C++ too often and haven't touched the engine source before so i went the route that made the most sense.\r\n\r\nThis is mostly for quality of life but someone brought it up to me that there might be performance benefits from doing this directly in C++ instead of GDScript however i haven't tested that.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-09-23T00:00:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-28T22:21:45Z","closed_at":"2025-09-28T22:19:17Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"955dd2bfac274c6193841f2b68af6b23b6bb0c86","assignee":null